{"name":"Dynamite","hex":"#ff4422","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dynamite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A sub-sitio in the sitio of Hilltop, barangay of Ambuclao, Bokod, Benguet, Philippines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dynamite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dynamite","blocks":[{"text":"Dynamite is an explosive made of nitroglycerin, sorbents, and stabilizers. It was invented by Swedish chemist Alfred Nobel in 1866 and patented the following year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Inserting_dynamite_into_hole.jpg/330px-Inserting_dynamite_into_hole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamite","wikidata":"Q80728"},{"title":"Dynamite (BTS song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Dynamite\" is a song recorded by South Korean boy band BTS, released on August 21, 2020, through Big Hit Entertainment and Sony Music Entertainment. It is the band's first song fully recorded in English. The song was written by David Stewart and Jessica Agombar and produced by Stewart. It has been described as an upbeat disco-pop song with elements of funk, soul, and bubblegum pop, and takes influence from 1970s music—it features snapping handclaps, echoing synths, and celebratory horns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/BTS_Dynamite_%28NightTime_Version%29.svg/330px-BTS_Dynamite_%28NightTime_Version%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamite_(BTS_song)","wikidata":"Q98073193"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nobels_Extradynamit_label.jpg/500px-Nobels_Extradynamit_label.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nobels_Extradynamit_label.jpg/1280px-Nobels_Extradynamit_label.jpg?utm